            "review_title": "Review at ONIGIRI CAFE NGON",
            "review_text": "Tori Goe\nChiba Prefecture, Japan47 contributions\n0\nIf you go to Da Nang, you should visit\nSep 2024 • Friends\nJapanese quality rice balls that you can eat in Da Nang. The staff, who understand Japanese, hold each one with their hearts. When it's crowded, the Owners themselves stand at the counter. \n\nYou should definitely ask for miso soup. The delicious broth is working, and I almost tear up.\n\nI was like, \"sate tuna mayo\" rice balls, rice balls with pickled plums. Then there was the octopus wiener, fried chicken.\nOnigiri, you can feel the sweetness of the rice anyway. They say it's an onigiri made by thoroughly researching how to cook Vietnamese rice.\nThe fried chicken and ready meals are hearty, too.\n\nMany of you visit if you are tired of foreign food, but my personal Recommendation is to visit on your first day in Da Nang. This is because the souvenir shops on the second floor often have people who can speak Japanese, so they can share attractive information that only residents know, such as information on sightseeing spots in Da Nang.\n\nIt's a very omnipresent place: good taste, good atmosphere, good convenience, good staff. Japanese food overseas? You may think so, but you should go!\nRead more\nTranslated from Japanese\nShow original\nWritten September 11, 2024",
